hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19216","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Muawiyah meaning Ibn Salih from al-Ala meaning Ibn al-Harith from Haram ibn Hakim from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what makes ghusl obligatory, about the fluid that comes after fluid, about prayer in my house and prayer in the mosque, and about eating with a menstruating woman. He said: Allah is not shy of the truth. As for me, when I do such and such, and he mentioned ghusl, he said: I perform wudu as my wudu for prayer, I wash my private part, then he mentioned ghusl. As for the fluid that comes after fluid, that is madhy, and every potent male emits madhy, so I wash my private part from that and perform wudu. As for prayer in the mosque and prayer in my house, you see how close my house is to the mosque, yet to pray in my house is dearer to me than to pray in the mosque, except a prescribed prayer. As for eating with a menstruating woman, then eat with her."
"19217","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us from al-Ala ibn al-Harith from Haram ibn Hakim from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about eating with a menstruating woman. He said: Eat with her."
